nt\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p1169.jpg?fit=1024%2C576&ssl=1","jetpack_sharing_enabled":true,"jetpack_shortlink":"https:\/\/wp.me\/p8u1BN-iR","jetpack-related-posts":[{"id":31,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/processing\/","url_meta":{"origin":1169,"position":0},"title":"Processing","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"The total signal latency, in+out, in the signal-flow is at around 8ms. This presents a challenge regarding timing and I had to choose the effects I use based some what on this. I did a quick run-through of available effects in Ableton Live and Max for Live and checked how\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"space echo","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?fit=718%2C295&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":395,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/12\/23\/music-bendik-hovik-kjeldsberg\/","url_meta":{"origin":1169,"position":1},"title":"Performing an electronic composition","date":"December 23, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"Bendik Hovik Kjeldsberg is studying composition at the same Academy as I am doing my master degree. He asked me to perform one of his compositions with him. Since the composition's nature is very electronic it presented some challenges when we were to perform it. Listen to the composition here,\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p395.jpg?fit=480%2C360&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":493,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/12\/24\/equipment-standard-audio-latency\/","url_meta":{"origin":1169,"position":2},"title":"Equipment Standard &#8211; Audio latency","date":"December 24, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"One of the first issues I wanted to look into when I started working on my master thesis was audio latency. Audio latency is the delay between when an audio signal enters and when it emerges from a system. Potential contributors to latency in an audio system include analog-to-digital conversion,\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/12\/latencyheader_l.jpg?fit=700%2C512&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":248,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/10\/music-ambience-project\/","url_meta":{"origin":1169,"position":3},"title":"Music &#8211; Ambience Project","date":"October 10, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"This is an excerpt from a two hour performance at the Norwegian Academy of Music early 2011. Everyone in my live electronics class were placed all over the school, playing ambient music. I was in the canteen. The whole session was improvised. I used only my computer running Ableton Live.\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p248.jpg?fit=640%2C360&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":35,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/controllers-launchpad\/","url_meta":{"origin":1169,"position":4},"title":"Controllers (launchpad)","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"I started with what I already had, a Launchpad from Novation. In the aspect of diversity and portability, this controller presents many advantages. You have 64 + 16 buttons (8x8)+(2x8) located at a fairly small space, and you can flip through pages which multiplies your number of buttons endlessly. You\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"launchpad","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/6.jpg?fit=550%2C550&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":25,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/signal-flow\/","url_meta":{"origin":1169,"position":5},"title":"Signal-flow","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"The audio from my EMFit based contact microphones goes into my sound card (Focusrite pro40), then to the DAW - Ableton Live, through desired effects and\/or to be stored on the hard drive, back to the sound card and out to a PA-system. Sound engineers usually treat my drums as\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"signal-flow","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/41.gif?fit=586%2C476&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]}],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1169"}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=1169"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1169\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1874,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/1169\/revisions\/1874"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1753"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1169"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=1169"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=1169"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","te